## Frequently asked questions

**Do I need a subscription to use a Nixplay frame?**
No. Every frame works with a free account (500 MB photo storage, 15-second videos, up to 5 frames). Nixplay Plus ($29.99/year) adds unlimited photo storage and longer videos.

**Can Nixplay frames play videos?**
Yes. Clips play with sound alongside photos: up to 15 seconds on the free plan, 1 minute on Basic, and 2 minutes on Plus.

**Can grandparents use it without an app?**
Yes. The frame can be preloaded before it is gifted. Relatives can send photos by email. The recipient only needs to plug it in and connect to Wi-Fi.

**Can several people send photos to one frame?**
Yes. Family members can share to the frame through the app, web, email, or shared albums.

**Does it work with Google Photos, iCloud, or Dropbox?**
Dropbox albums sync automatically. [VERIFY: current Google Photos, iCloud, Facebook, and Instagram support by plan. Product pages mention Instagram, Facebook, and Alexa with a paid subscription.]

**Does Nixplay work outside the US?**
Yes. Nixplay has stores for the US, UK, Germany, and Canada, and frames can receive photos from anywhere in the world.

**What sizes are available?**
10.1", and 15.6".

**Is my data private?**
Photos are stored securely in the USA, and Nixplay is CCPA and GDPR compliant. Privacy policy: https://www.nixplay.com/pages/privacy-policy

